# HOW LONG EACH LAYER'S DEMAND SURVIVES BEING UNANSWERED, OR THE TYPED REASON NOBODY KNOWS.
# One row per layer: the span a queued order stays an order, and who owns its edge.
#
# ⭐⭐⭐ IT IS THE HALF OF THE TIME AXIS THE SCHEMA FILED AS MISSING. `pm:Divisibility` sits on
#    `Nameplate`, so `window` is the SUPPLY's duty cycle, and its own annotation says the
#    mirror -- demand with a lifetime -- is a fact about DEMAND and names `Layer/timeSlack` as
#    where it would go "if demand ever gains structure". `pm:Demand/patience` is that
#    structure, and this relation is the half that was previously unaskable.
#
# ⛔⛔ A PATIENCE IS NOT A TIME SLACK AND THE UNITS ARE HOW YOU TELL. A slack is quoted in the
#    unit of the shares it bounds -- `slack_unit_mismatch` requires it -- and a patience is a
#    span of time that bounds no shares. `merge-holding-composition`'s `shift-line` files both
#    and they carry the SAME NUMBERS in different units, because that layer's unit is service
#    time so the wait and the queue ahead of you are one quantity. The document argues exactly
#    that in a comment. It is a fact about that layer and not a licence to fold the two.
#
# ⭐⭐ THE RANGE AND ITS LICENCE ARE TWO COLUMNS. A shop knows the impatient customer leaves at
#    three minutes and the last at ten; that is the claim. "Service within five minutes" is a
#    NEGOTIATED EDGE on it, and `boundOrigin` is where an edge says whose it is. Reading the
#    two together is the difference between renegotiating a term and measuring again.
#
# ⛔ `absent reason="none"` IS ZERO PATIENCE, not a missing column: demand that leaves the
#   moment it is not served. `merge-holding-composition` describes an `on-call` part that "does
#   not survive being held at all" -- that is this state, and until the element existed it had
#   nowhere to be filed but a slack's absence.
-- pm:Demand/pm:patience, beside the demand it qualifies.
SELECT l.filing, l.layer,
       l.patience_low, l.patience_mode, l.patience_high, l.patience_unit,
       l.patience_origin, l.patience_absent,
       l.demand_unit
FROM pm.layer l
